{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_cqzni3hwf23h5uki4zwvfy2zzg7byucmnldsplwnmmt5epakllya","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tests pass. Summary of what was implemented:\n\n1. **`tf_header_read`** — Validates buffer size (≥32), checks `PSEQ` magic bytes, decodes all header fields (offsets, versions, counts, compression type, sequence UID) using little-endian byte ordering. Compression type is masked to lower 4 bits and validated.\n\n2. **`tf_compression_block_read`** — Validates buffer size (≥8) and decodes `first_frame_id` and `size` as little-endian u32s.\n\n3. **`tf_var_header_read`** — Validates buffer size (>4), decodes `size` and `id` fields, validates the size, and copies the variable value into `vd` if non-empty (matching the C `vd != NULL` check).\n\n4. **`tf_channel_range_read`** — Validates buffer size (≥6) and decodes two 24-bit little-endian integers for `first_channel_number` and `channel_count`.\n\nI added `<'a>` lifetime parameters to tie the input buffer lifetime to the optional `ep` end-pointer slice — this was necessary for the `ep` slice to point into `bd`, mirroring the C pointer semantics. No `unsafe`, no FFI, and the implementation uses pure-Rust little-endian decoding via `u16/u32/u64::from_le_bytes`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":582,"cache_read_input_tokens":32765,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":582,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4cde0a42-0dce-4e95-9a4a-130b80980ac5","uuid":"22a63b7e-c192-46e4-b5bb-20fbdc36cf6f"}
